{
    "background_story": "Rayden was a renowned architect celebrated for his innovative designs that blended functionality with aesthetics. His magnum opus was the grand entrance hall of the city's new museum, featuring a majestic column that seemed to defy gravity. The column, dubbed 'Eternal Pillar,' was a marvel of engineering, rising 30 feet into the air without any visible support. Rayden's design not only added an air of grandeur to the museum but also created a sense of community, as people from all walks of life gathered to marvel at the column's beauty. As Rayden's fame grew, so did his fascination with the ancient structures that inspired his work. He spent years studying the ruins of Greece and Rome, seeking to understand the secrets behind their timeless columns. Rayden's passion for columns became a hallmark of his career, earning him the nickname 'The Column King.'",
